.TH "CarnivoreBot Contributor Documentation" 1 0000-00-00 Subsystems:Core core.dc

.SH PURPOSE
The core.dc subsystem handles communication between the CarnivoreBot code and discord.py.

For example, it handles moving tasks involving discord.py from feature threads onto the main thread, as is required by the discord.py API.

Used by: \fIfeat(1)\fR

.SH PUBLIC API
The API intended to be used by the rest of the project - specifically \fIfeat(1)\fR - is the following:

.P
.in +4n
.EX
import discord

@fnTypes.public
def registerCommand(cmd: str, handler: Callable[[discord.Message], Coroutine], includePrefix: bool = True):
    ...

@fnTypes.public
def registerHandler(event: Literal['onMessage'], handler: Callable[[discord.Message], Coroutine]):
    ...

@fnTypes.public
def runDiscord(cr: Coroutine) -> asyncio.Future:
    ...
.EE
.in
.P

.SS SYNTAX

\# for registerCommand
.P
.in +2n
.EX
@fnTypes.public
def registerCommand(cmd: str, handler: Callable[[discord.Message, list[str]], Coroutine], includePrefix: bool = True):
    ...
.EE
.P

.in +4n
\fBParameters\fR
.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBcmd: str\fR \- Defines the command name (ex. \f[CR]\fB"ping"\fR)

.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBhandler: Callable[[discord.Message, list[str]], Coroutine]\fR \- Defines the function to be called with the discord message and a shell-like-split version of the message's content, which returns an awaitable \f[CR]\fBCoroutine\fR

.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBincludePrefix: bool = True\fR \- Defines whether the command needs to be called with or without the prefix defined in \f[CR]\fBconfig.toml\fR. Default: \f[CR]\fBTrue\fR

.in

.in
.P
\# for registerCommand

\# for registerHandler
.P
.in +2n
.EX
@fnTypes.public
