    ...
.EE
.P

.in +4n
\fBParameters\fR
.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBevent: str\fR \- the event name to register a handler for

.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBhandler: Callable[[discord.Message], Coroutine]\fR \- the handler to be called with the discord message triggering the event, which returns an awaitable \f[CR]\fBCoroutine\fR

.in
.P
\# for registerHandler

\# for runDiscord
.P
.in +2n
.EX
@fnTypes.public
def runDiscord(cr: Coroutine) -> asyncio.Future:
    ...
.EE
.P

.in +4n
\fBParameters\fR
.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBcr: Coroutine\fR \- the coroutine to push onto the main thread's event loop via \f[CR]\fBasyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe\fR

.in -4n  \# idk why this is needed but it is needed
\fBReturn Value\fR
.IP "" 8
\f[CR]\fBasyncio.Future\fR \- an awaitable Future. When awaited, it will await the coroutine that was pushed onto the main thread's event loop. Created via \f[CR]\fBaio.wrap_future\fR
