    ...
.EE
.P

.in +4n
\fBParameters\fR

.in +4n
\f[CR]\fBmsg: str\fR \- the message to split

.in -4n
\fBReturn Value\fR

.in +4n
\f[CR]\fBlist[str]\fR \- the message after being split with shell-like syntax

.in -4n
\fBNotes\fR

.in +4n
1. \f[CR]\fBshlexSplit\fR uses the \f[CR]\fIshlex\fR library to split the message

2. If splitting via \f[CR]\fIshlex\fR fails, the function falls back to splitting the message naively by spaces

